# Migration SQL files are hashed by sqlx (via tauri-plugin-sql) to detect
# changes. The hash is computed over the raw bytes, so CRLF vs LF line endings
# produce DIFFERENT checksums for byte-identical SQL. Without this, a Windows
# dev build (CRLF checkout) and a CI build (LF) disagree on the checksum and the
# app fails to start with "migration N was previously applied but has been
# modified". Pin these files to LF everywhere so every build agrees forever.
src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
